# APRS-IS TNC2 monitor-format sample corpus.
#
# One packet per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# These are representative, printable-safe examples covering the v1 data types.
# Binary-heavy packets (some Mic-E encodings) are better captured by the
# aprs-capture tool against a live APRS-IS feed.

# Uncompressed position, no timestamp, no messaging
N0CALL-9>APRS,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1:!4903.50N/07201.75W-Test 001234
# Uncompressed position, no timestamp, messaging capable
K7ABC-1>APRS,TCPIP*:=4717.44N/12220.61W-PHG5130/Test station
# Position with UTC timestamp
W1AW>APRS:/092345z4903.50N/07201.75W-Somewhere
# Position with timestamp, messaging capable
N0CALL>APRS:@092345z4903.50N/07201.75W-Msg station
# Southern/western hemisphere
N0CALL-5>APRS:!3327.50S/07043.00W-Santiago
# Compressed position
N0CALL-7>APRS:!/5L!!<*e7>7P[
# Mic-E position (destination encodes latitude)
N0CALL-7>S32UVT:'(_fn"Oj/
# Message
N0CALL>APRS::BLN1     :test message{123
# Message acknowledgement
N0CALL>APRS::N0CALL   :ack{123
# Object (live, with position)
N0CALL>APRS:;OBJECT   *111111z4903.50N/07201.75WrTest
# Object (killed)
N0CALL>APRS:;OBJECT   _111111z_Gone
# Item
N0CALL>APRS:)ITEM!4903.50N/07201.75Wr
# Status
N0CALL>APRS:>Hello from the field
# Telemetry
N0CALL>APRS:T#005,199,000,255,073,123,01101001
# Weather (positionless, with timestamp)
N0CALL-13>APRS:_100905zc220s004g005t077r000p000P000h50b10135
# Station capability
N0CALL>APRS:<IGATE,MSG_CNT=1
# Query
N0CALL>APRS:?APRS?
# Maidenhead grid locator
N0CALL>APRS:[FN20wa]
# Third-party traffic
N0CALL>APRS:}W1AW>APRS:>relayed status
# User-defined
N0CALL>APRS:{USERDEF
